  "answer": "Based on the NAWE website, the authors who contributed articles to **Writing in Education, Vol. 33 – \"Writing & Location\"** are:\n\n1. **Bryan Podmore** — two articles: \"A Risky Business This Writing?\" and \"Crashing through the Fourth Wall\"\n2. **Sarah Wardle** — two articles: \"Audere Est Facere\" and \"Reflections on Memory and Identity\"\n3. **Martin Goodman** — \"Location and Dislocation - a Writer's Use of Place\"\n4. **Fred Sedgwick** — \"Primary Children Writing in the Grip of Shakespeare\"\n5. **Paul Munden** — \"Text and Context\"\n6. **Maggie Butt** — \"The View from Here\"\n7. **Keith Bennett** — \"Welcome to Maribor\"\n8. **Carl Tighe** — \"Worlds in War: War in Words\"\n\nThat's 8 distinct authors contributing 10 articles total in this volume. (Note: Vol. 31 was also themed \"Writing & Location\" — a different issue — but you asked specifically for Vol. 33.)",
